   "subject": "Bayesian model selection and GoF in Multi sp. Occupancy models",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">Hello all,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">I&#39;m conducting multi-species occupancy models with covariates. Still figuring out how to include time effect (but that&#39;s part of another discussion). </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">Now I&#39;m evaluating alternatives to conduct GoF and model selection under a Bayesian framework... always falling into this trap!</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">GoF: I understand Bayesian p-value is uninformative with a binary response (z in occupancy models)... so I assume I have to discard that one. There are several examples in AHM1 for N... but not for Z. Any other alternatives?</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">Model Selection: Using Kuo Mallick indicator variable method seems to have several complications, and not sure how to approach them. I feel AHM1 is clear about it, but it gets rough for me to code the suggested joint priors to alleviate computational problems caused by independent priors (no coding example in the book). </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">Any suggestions, thoughts, or code example for non-expert programmers?   </div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br></div><div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">​Thanks!</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:small;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Andrea​</div><br></div>-- <br><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"border-collapse:collapse;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><font face=\"georgia, serif\"><font><div><span style=\"border-collapse:collapse;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><font>---</font></span></div>Andrea Paula Goijman, Ph.D</font></font></span><div><span style=\"border-collapse:collapse;color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><font face=\"georgia, serif\"><font>Cell 54 11 15 6293 6214<br></font><div><font>US Cell (always reachable) <a href=\"tel:(706)%20389-4356\" value=\"+17063894356\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">706 389 4356</a><br></font></div></font></span></div></div></div>\r\n</div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
