     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:blue\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,serif;color:blue\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hmec...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hmec...@googlegroups.com</a>] <b>On Behalf Of </b>Andrea Goijman<br><b>Sent:</b> Wednesday, April 27, 2016 10:15 AM<br><b>To:</b> hmecology: Hierarchical Modeling in Ecology &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hmec...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br><b>Subject:</b> Bayesian model selection and GoF in Multi sp. Occupancy models<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Hello all,<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">I&#39;m conducting multi-species occupancy models with covariates. Still figuring out how to include time effect (but that&#39;s part of another discussion). <u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Now I&#39;m evaluating alternatives to conduct GoF and model selection under a Bayesian framework... always falling into this trap!<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">GoF: I understand Bayesian p-value is uninformative with a binary response (z in occupancy models)... so I assume I have to discard that one. There are several examples in AHM1 for N... but not for Z. Any other alternatives?<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Model Selection: Using Kuo Mallick indicator variable method seems to have several complications, and not sure how to approach them. I feel AHM1 is clear about it, but it gets rough for me to code the suggested joint priors to alleviate computational problems caused by independent priors (no coding example in the book). <u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Any suggestions, thoughts, or code example for non-expert programmers?   <u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p></div><div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">​Thanks!<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\">Andrea​<u></u><u></u></span></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">-- <u></u><u></u></p><div><div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,serif;color:#222222\">-