     1,
     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Ha, Kristin Broms has been very productive indeed ! Hadn’t known about that one either.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Best regards  -- Marc<u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"DE\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Von:</span></b><span lang=\"DE\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">andrea....@gmail.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">andrea....@gmail.com</a>]\r\n<b>Im Auftrag von </b>Andrea Goijman<br>\r\n<b>Gesendet:</b> Mittwoch, 27. April 2016 16:31<br>\r\n<b>An:</b> Chris SUtherland<br>\r\n<b>Cc:</b> hmecology: Hierarchical Modeling in Ecology<br>\r\n<b>Betreff:</b> Re: Bayesian model selection and GoF in Multi sp. Occupancy models<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\">That&#39;s perfect!! Thanks Chris, I&#39;ll take a look at it!<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\">Andrea<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">On Wed, Apr 27, 2016 at 11:24 AM, Chris SUtherland &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">chris...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:blue\">Hi Andrea,</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:blue\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:blue\">Perfect timing. Kristin Broms has just published this neat paper:</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:blue\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:blue\">Model selection and assessment for multi-species occupancy models</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:blue\"><a href=\"http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1890/15-1471.1/abstract\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1890/15-1471.1/abstract&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792495100981000&amp;usg=AOvVaw23Hk2KCTtBm3_p_2Dfjfg8\">http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1890/15-1471.1/abstract</a></span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:blue\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:blue\">Seems like this should be just what you need, right?</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:blue\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:blue\">Chris</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:blue\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Garamond&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:blue\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">\r\n<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hmec...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hmec...@googlegroups.com</a>]\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Andrea Goijman<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Wednesday, April 27, 2016 10:15 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> hmecology: Hierarchical Modeling in Ecology &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hmec...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> Bayesian model selection and GoF in Multi sp. Occupancy models</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\">Hello all,</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\">I&#39;m conducting multi-species occupancy models with covariates. Still figuring out how to include time effect (but that&#39;s\r\n part of another discussion). </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\">Now I&#39;m evaluating alternatives to conduct GoF and model selection under a Bayesian framework... always falling into\r\n this trap!</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\">GoF: I understand Bayesian p-value is uninformative with a binary response (z in occupancy models)... so I assume I have\r\n to discard that one. There are several examples in AHM1 for N... but not for Z. Any other alternatives?</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\">Model Selection: Using Kuo Mallick indicator variable method seems to have several complications, and not sure how to\r\n approach them. I feel AHM1 is clear about it, but it gets rough for me to code the suggested joint priors to alleviate computational problems caused by independent priors (no coding example in the book). </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\">Any suggestions, thoughts, or code example for non-expert programmers?   </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\">​Thanks!</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\"> </span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:black\">Andrea​</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"> <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">--\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:#222222\">---</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:#222222\">Andrea Paula Goijman, Ph.D</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:#222222\">Cell 54 11 15 6293 6214</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Georgia&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;;color:#222222\">US Cell (always reachable)\r\n<a href=\"tel:706%20389%204356\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\">706 389 4356</a></span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"color:#888888\">--\r\n<br>\r\n*** Three hierarchical modeling email lists ***<br>\r\n(1) unmarked: for questions specific to the R package unmarked<br>\r\n(2) SCR: for design and Bayesian or non-bayesian analysis of spatial capture-recapture<br>\r\n(3) HMecology (this list): for everything else, especially material covered in the books by Royle &amp; Dorazio (2008), Kéry &amp; Schaub (2012), Kéry &amp; Royle (2015)<br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;hmecology: Hierarchical Modeling in Ecology&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">hmecology+...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">\r\nhmec...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nVisit this group at <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/group/hmecology\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www